HST Office: Flash Fill (Tự điền nhanh, Ctrl+E) in HST Sheets, like the leading spreadsheet application
(owner 18/11: mandatory in 1.0.3). LibreOffice has no such feature; the logic is HST-owned
(SPDX LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary), LibreOffice files only get the command hooks.

- sc/source/core/hst/hstflashfill.cxx (sc/inc/hstflashfill.hxx): the inference. A program is a sequence of
  constant text and parts of the source columns (whole text, n-th word / run of letters / run of digits,
  n-th field between delimiters, text before or after the first or last delimiter, a word's first letter;
  counted from the start or the end), each as is, UPPER, lower or Proper. Programs that produce the first
  example are searched cheapest first; the cheapest that produces all other examples wins, the one
  filling more rows among equally cheap ones. Vietnamese letters with diacritics (also decomposed) count
  as letters.
- sc/source/ui/hst/hstflashfillcommand.cxx: .uno:FlashFill (SID_HST_FLASH_FILL) fills the empty cells of the
  cursor's column in its data region from the other columns, one undo step; a header row that does not
  follow the pattern is skipped; numbers stay numbers when the examples are numbers, otherwise text
  (keeps leading zeros). A message when there is no data or no pattern.
- Data menu (after Text to Columns) and command search; Ctrl+E in Sheets (was Center, still on the
  ribbon and in Format Cells; Excel's key). The ribbon button follows the ribbon refactor.
- Strings and Vietnamese translations (sc/messages.po, officecfg UI.po against the pristine tarball).

Test: CppunitTest_sc_hst_flash_fill (inference cases: Vietnamese names, joining columns, numbers,
dates, phone digits, case changes, initials, two examples, no pattern; the command with header row,
undo and numbers), scripts/check-keytips-parity.py (Ctrl+E row).
